    "narrative": "As we navigate the tail end of the 2026 campaign, the Austin Waves lineup centers on a high-upside matchup against Colorado, where **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) emerges as our primary engine. With a favorable 4.98 xERA from Ryan Feltner and a significant boost from his projected clean-up spot and dynamic platoon advantage, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our clear-cut top play. He is flanked by **Drake Baldwin** (68.36), who maintains elite efficiency out of the leadoff spot against Nick Martinez, and **Heliot Ramos** (65.44). **Heliot Ramos** is particularly intriguing; while his platoon dynamics are neutral, the slow delivery of Feltner offers a hidden edge for his speed-dependent profile, which is critical given our aggressive pursuit of Stolen Bases in this Roto format.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved **Dominic Smith** (58.33), who sits on the cusp of our \"Strong\" start threshold. While his score is bolstered by a +7% platoon edge, he narrowly squeezed into the starting rotation over other bench alternatives; his consistency against Martinez makes him a high-floor plug despite his middle-of-the-order positioning. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Sam Antonacci** (52.11). He faces a stiff test against Jared Jones (3.57 xERA), but his leadoff positioning and modest platoon benefit keep him in play as a marginal starter. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Miguel Vargas** (45.90); his involvement is strictly a volume play based on his projected #2 spot, but the matchup against Jones\u2019s elite stuff makes him a volatile asset today.\n\nBeyond our active starters, the bench remains static, as elite pillars like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are all idle due to scheduled off-days. We are maintaining our patient approach with **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains safely stashed on the IL. As we monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" tags for **Miguel Vargas**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Sam Antonacci**, ensure that any late defensive changes do not push our middle-order hitters into unfavorable sub-optimal slots. All eyes are on the Colorado matchup to provide the offensive spark we need to maintain our pace in the standings.",
